# Linking JXR Files to Javadocs

Each generated JXR page has a "View Javadoc" link to the Javadoc page of the same class. The link is on by default
and points to the `apidocs` directory of the site (`testapidocs` for the test sources), where the
[Javadoc Plugin](https://maven.apache.org/plugins/maven-javadoc-plugin/) writes its reports. Add the Javadoc Plugin to
the `<reporting>` section next to the JXR Plugin and the links resolve without further configuration.

If the Javadoc lives somewhere else, set `javadocLocation` (for `jxr:jxr` and `jxr:aggregate`) or
`testJavadocLocation` (for `jxr:test-jxr` and `jxr:test-aggregate`):

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <reporting>
    <plugins>
      ...
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-jxr-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          ...
          <javadocLocation>/path/to/javadocs</javadocLocation>
          ...
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  ...
  </reporting>
  ...
</project>
```

The plugin writes the link whether or not the Javadoc exists. If the site has no Javadoc, turn the link off so the
pages do not point to missing files:

```xml
<configuration>
  <linkJavadoc>false</linkJavadoc>
</configuration>
```
